{
 "source": "E. Di Lucente, M. Simoncelli, N. Marzari, Phys. Rev. Research 5, 033125 (2023); Materials Cloud Archive 5jsfj-cdg70 (CC BY 4.0)",
 "archive_readme": "Data related to the thermal properties of the three Fe-, Co- and Ir- families of \nfilled and unfilled skutterudites.\n\nIn each of the three folders there are:\n\n- Folder of the unfilled skutterudite\n- Folder of the related Yb-filled skutterudite\n\nIn each of these two there are:\n\n- Folder with the optimized geometry\n- Folder with the DFPT phonons\n- Folder with the computed 3rd-order force constants through ShengBTE (thirdorder.py)\n- Folder with the HipHive protocol for computing 3rd-order force constants\n- Folder with Phonopy run of the mean square displacement (MSD)\n- Folder with Phonopy run of the projected phonon density of states (PDOS)\n\nFor the case of YbFe4Sb12 we have also antiferromagnetic (AFM) calculations\n\nEach HipHive folder has inside the Phono3py calculation of thermal properties",
